# Line-ending policy (H3, ported from the call-data-reporting repo, where a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true once turned 7 tests red with no
# real defect). This repo has two CRLF-sensitive artifacts of its own: the
# split manifest's per-declaration SHA ledger (test/client/server-split-
# manifest.json) hashes source TEXT, and scripts/counts.mjs compares the
# generated block in CLAUDE.md byte-for-byte. A rewritten line ending fails
# both while looking like drift. The tree was already LF-clean when this
# landed (git ls-files --eol showed no CRLF), so normalization rewrites
# nothing -- it pins the state rather than changing it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF regardless: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look
# for an interpreter named "bash\r" ("bad interpreter"). Covered by the rule
# above; stated because it is the one case where CRLF breaks execution.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets, should any be committed (screenshots under docs/ already
# exist as PNGs): never normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
